#!/usr/bin/python3
"""One stale PREPARING-lease disposal for the fixed-capture B7 package. No apply.

The defined exit for a B7 apply that failed before migration-transaction.json existed.
Admits exactly two lease identities, each bound to its own frozen material:
  1. the pinned 2026-10-06 stale lease (binding canonical-sha == LEGACY_BINDING_SHA,
     material = the 20261006 parent candidate pins + its exact stale-seed pin), or
  2. a lease whose binding hashes/paths match THIS sealed package (material = this
     package's pins; the seed must be the worker-generated seed bound to this lease's
     own stage by its codeDigests tree digests).
Then proves zero production mutation under the lease (the receipt states the exact
checked scope) and removes ONLY the lease's own objects: placement stage, seed, placed
public artifacts, holder + lock dir. Any drift refuses before the first unlink. A
transaction file that exists is never disposed here; it keeps its own recovery path.

Delta vs the reviewed v2 entry (DELTA-REVIEW 2026-10-07, B1-B4):
  B1 the original holder's real mutex is taken on the holder open-file-description
     (flock LOCK_EX|LOCK_NB, the same mutex the original worker holds) and stays held
     until every namespace removal and fsync is complete; a live lock is refused, and
     holder inode/nonce and lock/root namespace identity are re-verified in the same
     protected operation before each mutation and before the final absence proofs.
  B2 the full stage/seed/artifact inventory is bound to the admitted lease's frozen
     material (the three part archives, the operation archive, the worker pin);
     unknown members refuse and are preserved; every removed object is re-verified by
     object identity (dev/ino) immediately before its unlink/rmdir, and by digest
     where bounded (seed, artifacts).
  B3 a per-operation journal inside the lease's own lock dir (fsync'd before the first
     mutation, updated at every step boundary, removed together with the lock) gives
     each unlink/rmdir/fsync/process-death boundary a bounded exit: rerunning this
     same entry resumes from the recorded facts and either completes or refuses; a
     fresh invocation never downgrades a prior partial operation to STOP_BEFORE_WRITE.
  B4 the legacy branch keeps the exact stale-seed SHA pin; the package-matched branch
     validates the seed structurally against this package's own template (only the
     three buildSeed mutations may differ) and binds its codeDigests to the actual
     stage trees, so a seed the new worker actually generated is admissible while an
     arbitrary seed is not.
All root paths arrive through main(); the checked functions take a Paths namespace so
the isolated fixture tests never touch the real filesystem layout.
"""
import base64
import contextlib
import fcntl
import hashlib
import json
import os
from pathlib import Path
import posixpath
import re
import stat
import sys
import tarfile

